START

1. Initialize Flask app and project directory paths

2. Define route: '/' (index)
   IF request is POST:
       Get project name, description, task type
       Save uploaded zip file
       Create project folders (data, models, results)
       Extract zip to 'data/' folder
       Organize folders: rename train2017 → train, val2017 → val
       Ensure structure: images/train, labels/train (and val)
       Create data.yaml file
       Render success message
   ELSE:
       Render home page with form

3. Define route: '/train' (model training)
   Get training configuration (epochs, batch size, etc.)
   Locate data.yaml
   Call YOLO training function from train_model.py
   Show training started/completed message

4. Define route: '/predict' (inference)
   Save uploaded image to data folder
   Call YOLO predict function from predict.py
   Return predicted image to frontend

5. Run Flask app

END
